# Copy this file to services/api/.env and fill in real values. That file is gitignored and must
# never be committed. scripts/start-api.ps1 loads it at startup; values already present in the
# environment take precedence, so this never overrides a real deployment's secret manager.

# AcoustID API key -- used by the rights gate's fingerprint check (app/acoustid/client.py).
#
# Without it, every lookup fails with "ACOUSTID_API_KEY is not set", and the gate holds every
# upload at pending_review rather than passing it. That is the CORRECT conservative behavior --
# a gate that cannot verify a fingerprint must not let audio through to a GPU -- but it means
# uploads appear to do nothing, and no track ever reaches the auto-processing pipeline.
#
# To get one (free): register an application at https://acoustid.org/new-application
#   - Requires an acoustid.org login (MusicBrainz account or an OpenID provider).
#   - "Application name" can be anything, e.g. songbox-dev. Version: 0.1. Application type: other.
#   - The value you want is the "API key" / client key shown after registering -- NOT your
#     account password and NOT a MusicBrainz token.
ACOUSTID_API_KEY=

# Single-user escape hatch for the rights gate. Default OFF.
#
# The gate holds anything it cannot positively clear -- a fingerprint that matches a commercial
# release, or a lookup it could not perform at all. That is correct for a service that accepts
# audio from strangers. On a personal install it is a dead end: a hold has no second human to
# escalate to, so every track stops at pending_review and nothing can ever be processed.
#
# Set to 1 on a personal, single-user machine to make the gate record its findings and pass
# anyway. The fingerprint lookup still runs and its real result is still written to
# fingerprint_matches, so the audit trail shows what the gate saw; only enforcement changes, and
# the stored reason says so explicitly.
#
# NEVER set this on a deployment serving more than one person. The gate is the only thing standing
# between such a deployment and processing content nobody has cleared.
SONGBOX_PERSONAL_MODE=

# Address the API binds to. Leave blank for uvicorn's loopback-only default (127.0.0.1), which is
# correct for plain local dev and fails closed.
#
# To reach this instance from your own other devices, join a Tailscale network and set this to
# THIS machine's Tailscale address (`tailscale ip -4`, e.g. 100.73.1.100). Bind that address
# specifically rather than 0.0.0.0: with 0.0.0.0 the only thing keeping these ports off whatever
# LAN you are on is a Windows Firewall rule scoped to the Private profile, and Windows stores that
# classification per network profile -- join one network it considers Private and the port opens to
# that entire LAN. Binding one address makes the kernel refuse those connections outright.
#
# While this is set, http://localhost:8000 will not answer on this machine; use the Tailscale
# address from here too.
SONGBOX_BIND_HOST=

# Extra origins the browser is allowed to call this API from, beyond the built-in
# http://localhost:3000. Comma-separated. Must be concrete origins -- "*" is rejected at startup,
# because combined with credentialed CORS it would grant every origin on the internet an
# authenticated handle on this API.
#
# Needed to reach this instance from another device: your phone loading the frontend at
# http://100.73.1.100:3000 needs THAT origin listed here, or the browser's CORS preflight silently
# blocks every request. Use the same 100.x address as SONGBOX_BIND_HOST (`tailscale ip -4`).
# Tailscale's MagicDNS name (http://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net:3000) works too.
#
# IMPORTANT -- use the SAME host form here as in apps/web/.env.local's NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL:
# both the 100.x IP, or both the MagicDNS name, never one of each. Different ports on one host are
# still same-site, so the SameSite=lax session cookie is sent; two different HOSTS are not, and the
# browser will silently withhold the cookie. Every authenticated request then 401s while CORS
# itself looks perfectly fine -- which reads as "login is broken", not "my two env vars disagree".
#
# This only ever needs a Tailscale (or other private-network) origin -- SONGBOX_PERSONAL_MODE
# assumes nobody outside your own devices can reach this instance at all. Do not add a public
# origin here without first setting SONGBOX_PERSONAL_MODE back to unset/0 and getting a real
# ACOUSTID_API_KEY, or you are exposing an unenforced rights gate to the internet.
SONGBOX_EXTRA_CORS_ORIGINS=

# Leave unset for local/Tailscale use. Setting this to "production" makes the session cookie
# Secure, which the browser then refuses to store over plain http:// -- so login silently stops
# working over a plain-HTTP Tailscale address, with no error to explain it.
SONGBOX_ENV=
